{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch484kh2Zb2QFUqTRBRdf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed the typo but haven't committed it yet. A single commit would break the nightly import.\n\n**Change:** There was one `wholsale` row in each of `data/2025-09.csv`, `data/2025-10.csv` and `data/2025-11.csv`. All three now read `wholesale`, so the diff is 3 lines. No other file had the typo, and `scripts/check.sh` passes.\n\n**Why I held the commit:** The README says the nightly import reloads only the data file for the month the commit message starts with. With one commit, say `2025-09: fix wholesale typo`, it would reload September only. October and November would keep `wholsale` in the imported data even though the files are fixed.\n\nWhich do you want?\n1. **Three commits**, one per month (`2025-09: …`, `2025-10: …`, `2025-11: …`). The import picks up all three. This is what I'd recommend.\n2. **One commit anyway**, if you'll reload October and November some other way, or if the import doesn't matter for this fix.\n\nThe edits are sitting unstaged in the working tree until you decide."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":450,"cache_read_input_tokens":22481,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":450},"output_tokens":351,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-64>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T04:58:51.233Z","request_id":"req_011Ch484kUtG5qHZ7ZpVR91j"}
